    456          /**
    457           *  @brief      Handle Mci events every Pwm interrupt.
    458           *
    459              @startuml{MCI_Class_A_State_Machine.png}
    460          
    461                  title Motor Control Interface - Main state machine
    462          
    463                  [*] --> MCI_INITIALIZING
    464          
    465                  MCI_INITIALIZING : Waits until data are reliable \nfrom either Class A and Class B
    466                  MCI_INITIALIZING --> MCI_FAILED : [Initialization timer expired]
    467                  MCI_INITIALIZING --> MCI_IDLE   : [No error found] AND\n[Class B in IDLE]
    468          
    469          
    470                  MCI_IDLE : Motor is idling.
    471                  MCI_IDLE : Entry / MCI_IDLE_ENTRY()
    472                  MCI_IDLE : Do / MCI_IDLE_PWM() - MCI_IDLE_2ND_PWM()
    473                  MCI_IDLE : Exit / MCI_IDLE_EXIT()
    474                  MCI_IDLE --> MCI_CLASS_B_STARTING   : [User requested to run] OR\n[User requested to manual control]
    475                  MCI_IDLE --> MCI_FAILED : [Any error found in either Class A or Class B]
    476          
    477          
    478                  MCI_CLASS_B_STARTING : Waiting for Class B to be ready,\ne.g. perform plausibility check.
    479                  MCI_CLASS_B_STARTING --> MCI_CLASS_B_STOPPING   : [User requested to stop]
    480                  MCI_CLASS_B_STARTING --> MCI_MANUAL_CONTROL     : [User requested to manual control] AND\n[Class A granted access to PWM]
    481                  MCI_CLASS_B_STARTING --> MCI_STARTING           : [User requested to run] AND\n[Class A granted access to PWM]
    482                  MCI_CLASS_B_STARTING --> MCI_FAILED             : [Any error found in either Class A or Class B]
    483          
    484          
    485                  MCI_CLASS_B_STOPPING : Waiting for Class B to be finish its checks,\ne.g. perform plausibility check.
    486                  MCI_CLASS_B_STOPPING --> MCI_IDLE               : [Class B is IDLE]
    487                  MCI_CLASS_B_STOPPING --> MCI_FAILED             : [Any error found in either Class A or Class B]
    488          
    489          
    490                  MCI_FAILED : Fault found in either inverter or motor
    491                  MCI_FAILED : Check and recover from failure
    492                  MCI_FAILED --> MCI_IDLE   : [Class B in IDLE] AND\n[All errors are cleared]
    493          
    494          
    495                  MCI_STARTING : Motor is performing activities before running control technique
    496                  MCI_STARTING : Entry / MCI_STARTING_ENTRY()
    497                  MCI_STARTING : Do / MCI_STARTING_PWM() - MCI_STARTING_2ND_PWM()
    498                  MCI_STARTING : Exit / MCI_STARTING_EXIT()
    499                  MCI_STARTING --> MCI_CLASS_B_STOPPING   : [User requested to stop]
    500                  MCI_STARTING --> MCI_RUNNING            : [MCI_STARTING_GUARD_EXIT() == TRUE]
    501                  MCI_STARTING --> MCI_FAILED             : [Any error found in either Class A or Class B]
    502          
    503          
    504                  MCI_RUNNING : Motor is controlled by FOC/DTC, e.g. automatic control.
    505                  MCI_RUNNING : Entry / MCI_RUNNING_ENTRY()
    506                  MCI_RUNNING : Do / MCI_RUNNING_PWM() - MCI_RUNNING_2ND_PWM()
    507                  MCI_RUNNING : Exit / MCI_RUNNING_EXIT()
    508                  MCI_RUNNING --> MCI_STOPPING            : [MCI_RUNNING_GUARD_EXIT() == TRUE]
    509                  MCI_RUNNING --> MCI_FAILED              : [Any error found in either Class A or Class B]
    510          
    511          
    512                  MCI_MANUAL_CONTROL : Motor is under manual control.
    513                  MCI_MANUAL_CONTROL : Entry / MCI_MANUAL_INJECTION_ENTRY()
    514                  MCI_MANUAL_CONTROL : Do / MCI_MANUAL_INJECTION_PWM() - MCI_MANUAL_INJECTION_2ND_PWM()
    515                  MCI_MANUAL_CONTROL : Exit / MCI_MANUAL_INJECTION_EXIT()
    516                  MCI_MANUAL_CONTROL --> MCI_CLASS_B_STOPPING     : [User requested to stop]
    517                  MCI_MANUAL_CONTROL --> MCI_FAILED               : [Any error found in either Class A or Class B]
    518          
    519          
    520                  MCI_STOPPING : Motor is controlled by class A and it is stopping.
    521                  MCI_STOPPING : Entry / MCI_STOPPING_ENTRY()
    522                  MCI_STOPPING : Do / MCI_STOPPING_PWM() - MCI_STOPPING_2ND_PWM()
    523                  MCI_STOPPING : Exit / MCI_STOPPING_EXIT()
    524                  MCI_STOPPING --> MCI_CLASS_B_STOPPING   : [MCI_STOPPING_GUARD_EXIT() == TRUE]
    525                  MCI_STOPPING --> MCI_FAILED             : [Any error found in either Class A or Class B]
    526          
    527              @enduml
    528           */

   \                                 In section .text, align 4, keep-with-next
